<%# What a tool hands back, by kind. Three shapes, so this is three
    paragraphs rather than sixty (docs/ABOUT_PLAN.md §3). %>
<% case tool.kind %>
<% when :draft %>
  <p class="text-sm text-soft">
    A written draft you own and can edit — saved into your notes, filed
    where it belongs, and yours to send or not send. Where a detail is
    missing it leaves a clearly marked blank rather than inventing one.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-soft">
    Alongside it: up to <%= Tool::Base::MAX_FOLLOW_UPS %> small follow-ups
    added to your tasks, and any real deadline it found put on your calendar
    as a dated reminder.
  </p>
<% when :plan %>
  <p class="text-sm text-soft">
    A goal, broken into tasks that each fit inside a day. The big thing you
    typed in one line comes back as an ordered list you can actually start
    on tomorrow morning, on your board with the rest of your work.
  </p>
<% when :chat %>
  <p class="text-sm text-soft">
    A conversation, kept for as long as you want it. It has already read the
    relevant part of what you've filed, so you can start in the middle
    instead of explaining your situation from scratch.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-soft">
  Nothing is sent anywhere, and nothing is filed you can't delete.
</p>
